sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 3 of the command development pipeline (verifying-commands skill). The author runs the command's cases on the nested fleet of the development environment, before pushing. Orbit's own Swamp runs the reset and verify workflows (workflow-proof-fleet-reset, -ready, -verify) and reaches into the task VM over SSH, like every other step. The Gateway only admits the request and mints tokens. The same cases and assertions run in CI (stage 4).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 3 · proof
  %% kind: pipeline.3-proof
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=amber
  participant AG as Author agent<br/>in the task VM
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>authorizes only
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>owns flow · state
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>outer VM
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>Gateway · 2 Nodes
  AG->>GW: Ask for the proof<br/>orbit proof:run COMMIT
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit proof:run COMMIT` for the command's cases
  %%> Built or not:
  %%> - built, with one case so far: the `firewall:allow` traffic case; every other command's cases are not built
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the request from a branch that is not pushed yet; `proof:run` takes only a commit on a branch of the repository today
  Note over GW: Admit the request<br/>trust check · cases
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the commit and selects the cases, as in the chart of `proof:run`
  %%> - records the operation for the CLI and web, and mints the tokens the run needs
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway only authorizes; Swamp owns the flow and its state
  GW->>SW: Start the proof run<br/>operation-proof-run
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - Orbit's own Swamp running the reset and verify workflows directly; today `bin/proof-fleet` starts a local Swamp inside the task VM
  SW->>VM: Reset the fleet<br/>workflow: proof-fleet-reset
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Swamp reaches into the task VM over SSH, like every other step; there is no `bin/proof-fleet` and no controller Swamp in the VM
  %%> - starts each independent run on a fresh nested fleet (stage 2), with the branch's code applied
  %%> - falls back to a full build when no ready copy is usable
  %%> - pushes the proof Swamp Club key from its vault into the nested Gateway, which runs its own Swamp as part of the Orbit under test
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the key is copied in at boot and never baked into an image; it is never stored on the outer task VM
  SW->>VM: Run the cases<br/>workflow: proof-fleet-verify
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the verify workflow runs each selected case against the nested fleet through the task VM, over SSH
  loop each case, in order
    SW->>NT: Check the starting state<br/>control probe
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - confirms the test setup works before the command runs, for example a healthy listener and a port that is blocked
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a broad unmanaged allowance must not let a case pass without the rule under test
    SW->>NT: Run the real CLI<br/>built from the tested commit
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - calls the command through its real interface: required arguments only, each flag, each error path
    NT-->>SW: Result<br/>exit status · output
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the public result in human and JSON output
    SW->>NT: Check the real effect<br/>record · Node · behavior
    %%> What it checks:
    %%> - the Gateway record, the observed Node state, and the promised effect, such as traffic that passes or stays blocked
    %%> - Doctor reports no drift for the records the case touched
    %%> - what must stay unchanged, including unmanaged resources
    SW->>NT: Repeat the request<br/>nothing changes
    %%> What it checks:
    %%> - a repeat adds no managed resource and changes no configuration; a documented skip returns its reason code
    SW->>NT: Clean up the case<br/>compare with the baseline
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - scoped cleanup, then compares the case's own database and firewall state with its start
    %%> - residue fails the case; an infrastructure failure is reported apart and never counts as a pass
  end
  alt every case passes
    SW-->>GW: Receipt<br/>PASS per case
    GW-->>AG: Receipt<br/>PASS per case
    %%> Result:
    %%> - one verdict per case with observations, Doctor findings and timings; the Gateway records it once; the author may push (stage 4)
  else a case fails or did not run
    SW--xGW: Receipt<br/>FAIL with output
    GW--xAG: Receipt<br/>FAIL with output
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the failed case with its output, without secrets; the author fixes and runs again
  end
  opt a new case is added
    Note over SW,NT: Prove the case can fail<br/>on an isolated checkout
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the mutation on an isolated checkout and confirms the functional assertion fails
    %%> - never mutates a live installation
    %%> Not built:
    %%> - exercising the CI gate with a known failing case (stage 4)
  end
